    {
      "id": "awzk3kw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.4 Panchayati Raj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rjut180",
      "content": "Odisha has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system as per the 73rd Constitutional Amendment:"
    },
    {
      "id": "v2lz63f",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Tier</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Body</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Village Level</p>",
            "<p>Gram Panchayat (Elected head: Sarpanch)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Block Level</p>",
            "<p>Panchayat Samiti (Elected head: Sabhapati)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>District Level</p>",
            "<p>Zila Parishad (Elected head: Adhyaksha)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: The total count of administrative districts in Odisha is 30.",
        "Important for prelims: Constitutional provisions regarding the Governor, Chief Minister, and High Court jurisdiction.",
        "Key topic: Structure and tiers of the Panchayati Raj framework in Odisha."
      ],
      "id": "fbxeqar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "whvxg85",
      "content": "Odisha has 6,794 Gram Panchayats, 314 Blocks, and 30 Zila Parishads (one per district). Urban local bodies include 114 Urban Local Bodies (ULBs)."
    },
